' diagram-type: sequence
@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title v0008 State Registry - Transit rotate (internal command only; AAD-bound ciphertext is never rewrap'd)

actor "Deployment Identity\n(state-registry crypto rotate)" as deployment_identity_user
database "State Registry" as state_registry_service
participant "OpenBao Transit" as openbao_transit_server
database "PostgreSQL\n(secret_versions.crypto_provider\n+crypto_migration_checkpoints per-row)" as state_registry_db

note over deployment_identity_user, state_registry_db
  rotate is the internal state-registry crypto rotate command
  authenticated by the deployment identity. NO new public HTTP
  endpoint. rotate creates a new latest key version; it does
  NOT raise min_encryption_version. AAD-bound ciphertext rows
  are NEVER rewrap'd because the documented
  /v1/<mount>/rewrap/<key_name> endpoint has no
  associated_data parameter. Historical rows remain bound to
  their embedded older key version. key_id is a deployment-time
  stable identifier mapped to (mount_path, key_name) through
  the secure runtime configuration; rotate does NOT change
  key_id.
end note

== rotate: create a new latest key version (no body, no documented response body) ==
deployment_identity_user -> state_registry_service : state-registry crypto rotate --key-name <key_name>
activate state_registry_service
state_registry_service -> openbao_transit_server : POST /v1/<mount>/keys/<key_name>/rotate
activate openbao_transit_server
openbao_transit_server --> state_registry_service : 204 No Content\n(no documented success body)
deactivate openbao_transit_server
state_registry_service -> openbao_transit_server : GET /v1/<mount>/keys/<key_name>\n(read the new latest version; do not log response body)
activate openbao_transit_server
openbao_transit_server --> state_registry_service : 200 {"data":{"keys":{"<old>":ts,"<new>":ts},\n"min_decryption_version":1,"min_encryption_version":1,...}}
deactivate openbao_transit_server
state_registry_service -> state_registry_service : audit crypto.rotate accepted\n(identifier-level metadata only:\nopaque key_id, previous_latest_version,\nnew_latest_version, request_id,\noutcome status class)
state_registry_service --> deployment_identity_user : accepted\n(identity-signed internal command)
deactivate state_registry_service

note over state_registry_service, openbao_transit_server
  rotate does NOT raise min_encryption_version or
  min_encryption_version. v0008 SHALL NOT advance
  min_decryption_version past any still-referenced key
  version; retiring historical versions requires an explicit
  future migration change.
end note

== Effect on historical AAD-bound ciphertext rows ==
state_registry_service -> state_registry_service : historical rows with embedded\nolder key version remain unchanged\nin secret_versions

note over state_registry_service, openbao_transit_server
  - new writes that do not specify key_version use the new
  latest version; their ciphertext embeds the new key version.
  - historical AAD-bound rows remain bound to their embedded
  older key version; they decrypt through the active provider
  using their original AAD byte string and the older key
  version.
  - the State Registry NEVER calls
  POST /v1/<mount>/rewrap/<key_name> for any row, because the
  documented rewrap endpoint has no associated_data parameter.
end note

== failure injection: ACL denial or sealed server ==
deployment_identity_user -> state_registry_service : internal command signed by\ndeployment identity\n(unauthorized / wrong-signed)
activate state_registry_service
state_registry_service -> state_registry_service : audit crypto.rotate rejected
state_registry_service --> deployment_identity_user : rejection recorded
deactivate state_registry_service

state_registry_service -> openbao_transit_server : POST /v1/<mount>/keys/<key_name>/rotate
activate openbao_transit_server
alt ACL denial
  openbao_transit_server --> state_registry_service : 403 {"errors":["permission denied"]}
else sealed server
  openbao_transit_server --> state_registry_service : 503 (sealed)
end
deactivate openbao_transit_server
state_registry_service -> state_registry_service : audit with provider_forbidden /\nprovider_unavailable outcome status class
state_registry_service --> deployment_identity_user : rotation failure recorded\n(no Transit detail; no plaintext disclosure)
@enduml